
# Wireshark

Wireshark is a network packet analyzer used to capture and analyze
network traffic in real time.

## Purpose
- To understand how data flows across a network
- To analyze packets such as TCP, UDP, DNS, and HTTP
- To identify source and destination IP addresses

## How It Works
Wireshark captures live network traffic from a selected interface
and displays the data in the form of packets for detailed analysis.

## Tool Used
- Wireshark

